1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:03,660
Wow, what a beautiful array of coding.

2
00:00:04,560 --> 00:00:06,300
Do you have any idea who wrote this?

3
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:07,880
Nope, no clue, I'm afraid.

4
00:00:08,720 --> 00:00:10,060
Here's your team, Ms. Kobayashi.

5
00:00:10,380 --> 00:00:11,700
Thanks, Selma, looks great.

6
00:00:12,160 --> 00:00:14,480
Oh no, why are you staring at the code I wrote?

7
00:00:15,060 --> 00:00:16,480
Is there something wrong with it?

8
00:00:16,860 --> 00:00:20,280
No, actually, I was just saying, I really...

9
00:00:20,280 --> 00:00:22,440
Wait, who wrote this again?

10
00:00:23,220 --> 00:00:24,540
That would be me, miss.

11
00:01:55,337 --> 00:01:57,597
And I can continue growing as well.

12
00:01:57,857 --> 00:02:00,977
Call me shallow, but I just assumed you'd be serving tea forever.

13
00:02:01,377 --> 00:02:04,617
What do you mean? You're the one who gave me all those books and told me to study!

14
00:02:05,077 --> 00:02:08,437
I guess you would have high specs being a dragon. Great work, Elma.

15
00:02:08,897 --> 00:02:09,957
This is amazing.

16
00:02:10,977 --> 00:02:13,257
Oh no! Are you praising me, miss?

17
00:02:13,397 --> 00:02:17,477
Yes, I am! This means we have another awesome fighting member on our team.

18
00:02:17,897 --> 00:02:18,857
Way to go, Elma.

19
00:02:20,157 --> 00:02:21,977
Thanks! All you have to do is leave it to me!

20
00:02:21,977 --> 00:02:23,977
Great! Could you start by handling this, then?

21
00:02:25,897 --> 00:02:27,957
And this? Oh, and this one, too.

22
00:02:28,857 --> 00:02:31,977
And this. And this one, this one, this one, and this one.

23
00:02:32,057 --> 00:02:32,957
We're counting on you!

24
00:02:33,097 --> 00:02:35,117
Hold on! That's too much!

25
00:02:35,237 --> 00:02:38,737
No, it's not. That's the amount of work you should be handling regularly.

26
00:02:40,317 --> 00:02:43,597
Kobayashi's the one who's been dealing with your share of assignments up until this point,

27
00:02:43,737 --> 00:02:44,817
while you were serving tea.

28
00:02:45,977 --> 00:02:49,177
She already has way too much on her plate without covering for you.

29
00:02:50,477 --> 00:02:52,517
Isn't that kind of incredible, Mr. Takuya?

30
00:02:52,517 --> 00:02:56,077
Yes, it is. She is our pillar of strength.

31
00:02:56,557 --> 00:02:57,037
Pillar?

32
00:02:58,077 --> 00:02:58,557
Mm-hmm.

33
00:02:59,237 --> 00:03:00,077
She's a pillar?

34
00:03:00,657 --> 00:03:01,197
I see.

35
00:03:02,717 --> 00:03:05,397
Miss Kobayashi, please stand up!

36
00:03:05,497 --> 00:03:07,117
I challenge you to a duel!

37
00:03:07,297 --> 00:03:07,437
Huh?

38
00:03:07,437 --> 00:03:09,817
Come on! Let's fight fair and square!

39
00:03:10,037 --> 00:03:10,477
Uh-huh.

40
00:03:11,097 --> 00:03:12,697
Where is this coming from?

41
00:03:13,177 --> 00:03:15,037
Maybe she's mad I gave her too much?

42
00:03:15,517 --> 00:03:17,437
Well, yeah, that's how Elma is!

43
00:03:18,057 --> 00:03:18,497
Huh.

44
00:03:18,997 --> 00:03:22,037
I think I kind of understand how you feel when she comes after you.

45
00:03:22,217 --> 00:03:24,817
She challenges me to the strangest matches, too.

46
00:03:25,077 --> 00:03:29,297
There were these tests of strength, then seeing whose tail was longer, and even speed eating.

47
00:03:29,777 --> 00:03:34,057
One time she challenged me to see which one of us could strip the clothes off of travelers first.

48
00:03:34,057 --> 00:03:39,997
Wait, so you were partners in crime? Now it makes sense why you were playing together all the time. You're actually friends.

49
00:03:40,317 --> 00:03:44,557
We are certainly not! Normally we would be trying to kill each other!

50
00:03:44,937 --> 00:03:50,477
Miss Kobayashi, please be careful around Elma. Your gaze is as sharp as those in the Chaos Faction!

51
00:03:50,897 --> 00:03:52,677
Is my resting face really that bad?

52
00:03:53,117 --> 00:03:56,617
Hello! You showed! You didn't run! Great!

53
00:03:56,617 --> 00:04:02,857
Well, I did consider taking some PTO. Can we please deal with this before we compete?

54
00:04:04,857 --> 00:04:08,577
It's one of the limited-time sweets from the station. A soft, sweet pudding.

55
00:04:10,257 --> 00:04:12,537
Normally this would be all it takes to satisfy Elma.

56
00:04:14,697 --> 00:04:16,757
No! I'll have it when I win the match!

57
00:04:16,837 --> 00:04:17,557
Whatever works.

58
00:04:17,557 --> 00:04:22,917
The winner will be whoever completes the most of this work that hasn't been touched since who knows when.

59
00:04:23,057 --> 00:04:23,517
All right!

60
00:04:23,777 --> 00:04:27,217
You say it hasn't been touched yet, but someone has to be responsible for it, right?

61
00:04:27,737 --> 00:04:27,997
Who?

62
00:04:28,377 --> 00:04:30,157
Ah, that would be me.

63
00:04:30,797 --> 00:04:33,597
I'm taking some time off. Going to Akibat with Fafnir.

64
00:04:33,817 --> 00:04:34,437
See you later!

65
00:04:35,437 --> 00:04:38,137
What a bastard. At least he works hard.

66
00:04:38,557 --> 00:04:42,437
I honestly can't tell if you're upset or grateful from the lack of tone in your voice.

67
00:04:43,277 --> 00:04:44,137
Shall we get started?

68
00:04:44,797 --> 00:04:45,457
Uh, yeah.

69
00:04:45,457 --> 00:04:49,897
Well, this might be the world's lamest competition.

70
00:04:52,317 --> 00:04:55,697
Doesn't matter if I win or lose. The work gets done either way.

71
00:04:56,957 --> 00:04:58,357
Time for lunch.

72
00:04:58,637 --> 00:05:00,257
You feel like doing some ramen again?

73
00:05:01,157 --> 00:05:02,577
Why don't you come with us, Elma?

74
00:05:02,857 --> 00:05:04,837
No, thanks. I still have a lot to do.

75
00:05:05,657 --> 00:05:10,637
Hmm. Beating a mere human like me can't possibly make you any happier, can it?

76
00:05:10,937 --> 00:05:12,937
If I upset you, I sincerely apologize.

77
00:05:12,937 --> 00:05:18,857
I'm not mad. And you shouldn't sell yourself short. Don't become a pillar, either.

78
00:05:19,277 --> 00:05:19,697
A pillar?

79
00:05:20,357 --> 00:05:25,297
That's right. I've watched way too many humans in despair become pillars in the other world.

80
00:05:25,837 --> 00:05:27,057
What does that mean?

81
00:05:27,757 --> 00:05:30,297
They support others by becoming a sacrifice themselves.

82
00:05:30,657 --> 00:05:31,817
Human sacrifices?

83
00:05:31,817 --> 00:05:37,377
The dragons of the Harmony Faction help humans, but many of my companions demand sacrifices in exchange.

84
00:05:38,257 --> 00:05:42,777
Those people became human pillars and died. I couldn't stand it if that happened to you.

85
00:05:42,777 --> 00:05:46,057
This conversation has taken an awfully dramatic turn.

86
00:05:46,437 --> 00:05:51,057
I feel like we're losing you to your work. You have to stop sacrificing yourself and your happiness here.

87
00:05:51,437 --> 00:05:53,557
The least you can do is allow me to lead the others.

88
00:05:54,457 --> 00:05:58,817
Elma, could you bring your head closer, then close your eyes?

89
00:05:59,077 --> 00:06:00,337
Huh? What do you mean?

90
00:06:00,617 --> 00:06:02,837
Miss Kobayashi, please, you already have Toru.

91
00:06:03,497 --> 00:06:07,157
But, um, if you want that from me too, I'm not one to tell you what to do.

92
00:06:07,157 --> 00:06:09,277
Wake up!

93
00:06:09,297 --> 00:06:10,697
Owens! Owens! Owens!

94
00:06:11,237 --> 00:06:13,117
What the heck's the matter with you?

95
00:06:14,517 --> 00:06:16,577
That's called an unnecessary concern.

96
00:06:17,137 --> 00:06:17,577
What?

97
00:06:18,697 --> 00:06:23,037
The world you live in now is different from the one you came from, so take some time to breathe.

98
00:06:23,397 --> 00:06:25,117
Don't go thinking everything is the same.

99
00:06:26,617 --> 00:06:29,277
There are no human sacrifices in modern Japan.

100
00:06:29,897 --> 00:06:33,217
Also, I still have my honor as your senior here, so lay off my work.

101
00:06:33,637 --> 00:06:34,357
I see.

102
00:06:34,357 --> 00:06:37,077
I think we should go ahead and end this competition.

103
00:06:37,757 --> 00:06:37,957
Yeah?

104
00:06:38,637 --> 00:06:38,957
Kay.

105
00:06:39,377 --> 00:06:41,557
I appreciate how concerned you were for me, though.

106
00:06:42,357 --> 00:06:43,037
Thank you, Elma.

107
00:06:44,257 --> 00:06:44,737
Sure.

108
00:06:45,417 --> 00:06:47,277
Another day, another yen, am I right?

109
00:06:47,877 --> 00:06:48,517
Okay, Elma.

110
00:06:48,957 --> 00:06:50,817
You're coming with us to have drinks tonight.

111
00:06:51,357 --> 00:06:51,657
Drinks?

112
00:06:52,177 --> 00:06:55,177
Yeah, Takya's already standing by at our usual watering hole.

113
00:06:56,237 --> 00:06:58,277
I bet it'll be fun to drink with everyone.

114
00:06:58,877 --> 00:06:59,517
Uh, yeah.

115
00:06:59,717 --> 00:07:02,577
And there are some things you can only talk about with liquid courage.

116
00:07:02,577 --> 00:07:03,577
Now I'm excited!

117
00:07:04,817 --> 00:07:06,297
And what's up with that outfit?

118
00:07:06,557 --> 00:07:06,857
Ew!

119
00:07:07,157 --> 00:07:08,877
You dragons really piss me off!

120
00:07:08,957 --> 00:07:10,397
You think you can wear whatever you want?

121
00:07:10,577 --> 00:07:10,917
Both!

122
00:07:10,997 --> 00:07:12,777
You can't just wear glasses for fun.

123
00:07:12,957 --> 00:07:14,477
Blindness is not a fashion statement!

124
00:07:14,797 --> 00:07:16,337
No one's tits are that huge!

125
00:07:16,377 --> 00:07:19,757
As one who wears glasses, I know there are big differences in sizes and frames.

126
00:07:19,837 --> 00:07:21,817
If you're gonna wear them, you need to take a frame as I thought first.

127
00:07:21,817 --> 00:07:22,537
I wanna go home.

128
00:07:22,537 --> 00:07:23,037
Yeah!

129
00:07:23,037 --> 00:07:23,117
Yeah!

130
00:07:27,337 --> 00:07:29,357
This is a popular collaboration cafe.

131
00:07:29,677 --> 00:07:31,297
We're pretty lucky it's emptier on weekdays.

132
00:07:33,297 --> 00:07:33,777
Yeah.

133
00:07:34,337 --> 00:07:35,517
Sorry for the wait.

134
00:07:36,017 --> 00:07:38,497
Here's a special bonus illustrated coaster you ordered.

135
00:07:39,677 --> 00:07:41,797
There are 15 types handed out at random.

136
00:07:42,277 --> 00:07:45,457
I need you to be my partner in gathering stuff until I can collect them all.

137
00:07:45,457 --> 00:07:47,517
Let's make it happen.

138
00:07:51,257 --> 00:07:52,137
That's scary.

139
00:07:52,877 --> 00:07:54,457
They're recruiting for patrols.

140
00:07:54,677 --> 00:07:56,957
Yeah, they asked me if I wanted to work for them.

141
00:07:57,077 --> 00:07:57,317
Huh?

142
00:07:57,317 --> 00:08:01,557
They were impressed with my skills after they saw me catch that thief in the shopping district.

143
00:08:02,117 --> 00:08:02,637
Right.

144
00:08:03,137 --> 00:08:04,677
That actually happened, didn't it?

145
00:08:06,557 --> 00:08:08,057
You think it would be safe?

146
00:08:09,177 --> 00:08:10,977
Sweet of you to worry about me!

147
00:08:11,677 --> 00:08:12,617
For others.

148
00:08:12,657 --> 00:08:14,057
Oh, damn it!

149
00:08:14,757 --> 00:08:16,577
Thanks so much for coming today, Toru.

150
00:08:17,257 --> 00:08:18,717
You're in normal clothes.

151
00:08:18,897 --> 00:08:19,837
What a surprise.

152
00:08:20,257 --> 00:08:22,957
Miss Kobayashi said I should wear more than just my uniform.

153
00:08:23,577 --> 00:08:26,197
So, um, how would you like me to patrol for you?

154
00:08:26,197 --> 00:08:29,917
All you have to do is walk around the area and see if you spot anything strange.

155
00:08:30,157 --> 00:08:31,897
It can be a little scary sometimes.

156
00:08:32,237 --> 00:08:34,997
There's nothing in any of the worlds that can scare me!

157
00:08:35,237 --> 00:08:37,197
I'm a chaos dragon born to be feared!

158
00:08:37,437 --> 00:08:38,357
Oh, that's so cute.

159
00:08:39,557 --> 00:08:41,777
Mrs. Sakibay, do you know any martial arts?

160
00:08:42,257 --> 00:08:43,397
No, nothing at all.

161
00:08:43,697 --> 00:08:46,137
So then you'd be a hindrance to me if something does happen.

162
00:08:47,777 --> 00:08:49,117
Nothing is going to happen.

163
00:08:49,477 --> 00:08:52,217
I promise this is one of the safest areas you could be in.

164
00:08:53,557 --> 00:08:54,797
A red zone already?

165
00:08:54,797 --> 00:08:56,917
Why today of all days?

166
00:08:58,357 --> 00:08:59,697
Miss Sakibay, are you all right?

167
00:09:00,797 --> 00:09:03,277
They're blocking the street and getting in the way, aren't they?

168
00:09:03,617 --> 00:09:04,817
We should go warn them.

169
00:09:05,497 --> 00:09:05,937
Maybe.

170
00:09:06,237 --> 00:09:07,217
Hey, you guys!

171
00:09:08,477 --> 00:09:10,837
You're disrupting the neighborhood by loitering here.

172
00:09:10,957 --> 00:09:12,237
Oh, are we?

173
00:09:12,697 --> 00:09:14,397
You got a problem with us?

174
00:09:14,517 --> 00:09:15,237
I sure do.

175
00:09:16,097 --> 00:09:18,417
What kind of species doesn't understand its own language?

176
00:09:18,417 --> 00:09:22,037
Quit screwing around with me!

177
00:09:22,037 --> 00:09:23,037
You idiot!

178
00:09:23,037 --> 00:09:24,917
It lashes out way too fast!

179
00:09:28,697 --> 00:09:35,757
I will only warn you one more time, so if you don't understand, then I will give up hope.

180
00:09:35,757 --> 00:09:37,217
Go away.

181
00:09:38,377 --> 00:09:40,717
You're going to recruit, picking a fight with us!

182
00:09:40,917 --> 00:09:42,557
Team Dragon Buster's out!

183
00:09:42,877 --> 00:09:45,097
That's the most obnoxious name I've ever heard.

184
00:09:45,657 --> 00:09:48,197
So, let's regroup and get back to our patrol.

185
00:09:48,977 --> 00:09:51,277
Do you know what you'll do if they come back for revenge?

186
00:09:51,497 --> 00:09:52,517
Uh, yeah.

187
00:09:52,697 --> 00:09:53,717
First, I'd make him.

188
00:09:54,517 --> 00:09:57,177
That's the most suspicious person I've ever seen in my life!

189
00:09:57,257 --> 00:09:57,477
Huh?

190
00:09:57,557 --> 00:09:58,837
What are you talking about?

191
00:09:59,057 --> 00:10:00,697
You're skipping out on work, aren't you?

192
00:10:00,757 --> 00:10:02,197
No, I got out early today.

193
00:10:02,757 --> 00:10:02,957
Huh?

194
00:10:03,577 --> 00:10:05,217
What's with that armband you're wearing?

195
00:10:05,577 --> 00:10:08,357
I'm on patrol to maintain the peace for the neighborhood, of course.

196
00:10:08,917 --> 00:10:09,297
Huh?

197
00:10:09,617 --> 00:10:10,217
You are?

198
00:10:10,557 --> 00:10:13,437
You're doing something to preserve the peace of the city we live in?

199
00:10:13,857 --> 00:10:15,017
That's what I said.

200
00:10:15,077 --> 00:10:15,717
Did I stutter?

201
00:10:19,717 --> 00:10:20,077
Really?

202
00:10:20,557 --> 00:10:22,597
I'm glad you finally found it for yourself.

203
00:10:22,597 --> 00:10:23,897
You believe in justice!

204
00:10:24,317 --> 00:10:24,537
Huh?

205
00:10:24,717 --> 00:10:25,917
This is the best news!

206
00:10:26,177 --> 00:10:27,957
From now on, you're in an agent of harmony!

207
00:10:28,337 --> 00:10:30,537
I would be so honored to help you with your patrol!

208
00:10:31,277 --> 00:10:33,717
I get the feeling you didn't understand what I said.

209
00:10:33,897 --> 00:10:35,917
Oh, are you saying you'd like to take my place?

210
00:10:36,137 --> 00:10:37,037
This is Saki-Ve!

211
00:10:37,197 --> 00:10:39,937
I mean, you told me I'd be a hindrance, didn't you?

212
00:10:40,877 --> 00:10:41,777
Oh, come on.

213
00:10:41,817 --> 00:10:44,177
I'm a bit more experienced at detecting evil than you are.

214
00:10:44,437 --> 00:10:46,217
You can ask me anything you want.

215
00:10:46,377 --> 00:10:48,617
I'd like to know the fastest way to get rid of you.

216
00:10:48,757 --> 00:10:49,697
Don't be embarrassed.

217
00:10:50,557 --> 00:10:52,457
There are times you can be super cute.

218
00:10:53,437 --> 00:10:54,417
So annoying.

219
00:10:55,337 --> 00:10:58,117
I'd like to know what it is exactly that you consider evil.

220
00:10:58,657 --> 00:11:02,677
I think it's okay to overlook some mild misconduct as long as it's not bothering anybody.

221
00:11:03,217 --> 00:11:04,737
Well, there's a book of laws, right?

222
00:11:04,897 --> 00:11:07,137
They shouldn't be doing anything against what's in there.

223
00:11:07,397 --> 00:11:08,317
Hurry up!

224
00:11:08,397 --> 00:11:09,857
It's about to turn red!

225
00:11:12,137 --> 00:11:12,917
Hold it!

226
00:11:12,917 --> 00:11:17,537
That's a traffic violation and a major fine to vote!

227
00:11:17,797 --> 00:11:19,737
Prepare to be punished, you wicked villains!

228
00:11:21,257 --> 00:11:22,177
Okay, okay.

229
00:11:22,297 --> 00:11:23,977
Take a deep breath and lay off the kids.

230
00:11:24,077 --> 00:11:24,437
What?

231
00:11:24,577 --> 00:11:25,817
Are you defending evil?

232
00:11:25,817 --> 00:11:28,017
I take it back, you are a chaos dragon!

233
00:11:28,477 --> 00:11:29,217
Calm down.

234
00:11:29,357 --> 00:11:32,637
If you're going to waste your time chasing after the little things, I'm going home.

235
00:11:32,817 --> 00:11:34,117
And what was that about punishment?

236
00:11:34,517 --> 00:11:36,017
Violence isn't going to solve anything.

237
00:11:36,397 --> 00:11:39,717
Oh, sorry, Toru, but you're starting to sound a lot like Miss Kobayashi.

238
00:11:40,397 --> 00:11:40,837
Really?

239
00:11:41,017 --> 00:11:41,917
You mean it, Alma?

240
00:11:42,317 --> 00:11:43,457
You get me, don't you?

241
00:11:43,477 --> 00:11:44,617
I had a feeling you did.

242
00:11:44,817 --> 00:11:45,297
Awkward.

243
00:11:46,017 --> 00:11:49,017
You keep focusing on the little things because you're walking without purpose.

244
00:11:49,637 --> 00:11:51,277
We must find the suspicious person.

245
00:11:51,497 --> 00:11:52,737
So what do they look like?

246
00:11:53,217 --> 00:11:57,077
Well, according to the flyer, they were dressed entirely in black and had long hair.

247
00:11:57,797 --> 00:12:00,977
He's also described as a tall man with sharp eyes and glasses.

248
00:12:00,977 --> 00:12:02,917
Oh, that sounds easy to identify.

249
00:12:03,657 --> 00:12:07,597
It says here he was last seen dancing on the streets on his way to an elementary school.

250
00:12:08,157 --> 00:12:08,657
I see.

251
00:12:08,657 --> 00:12:10,217
So, kind of like that?

252
00:12:10,697 --> 00:12:12,437
Yeah, exactly like that.

253
00:12:14,457 --> 00:12:16,077
What is the meaning of this?

254
00:12:17,037 --> 00:12:20,077
I was going over my choreography for an event with Takia.

255
00:12:20,537 --> 00:12:22,237
Why do you have to do it out here?

256
00:12:22,577 --> 00:12:24,057
Because our room is too small.

257
00:12:24,457 --> 00:12:28,457
Try to remember you're a fearsome dragon and do your best to avoid suspicious behavior.

258
00:12:29,017 --> 00:12:30,097
She's right, Faf.

259
00:12:30,177 --> 00:12:31,637
You need to be more self-aware.

260
00:12:32,057 --> 00:12:32,697
And you too?

261
00:12:33,097 --> 00:12:34,537
We're patrolling the streets.

262
00:12:34,697 --> 00:12:35,397
Excellent work.

263
00:12:35,397 --> 00:12:41,577
A chaos faction and a harmony faction member working together in a world that seems determined

264
00:12:41,577 --> 00:12:43,237
to drive everyone in it crazy.

265
00:12:43,637 --> 00:12:46,137
Yet you seem to be the only one here bothered by it.

266
00:12:46,277 --> 00:12:48,637
And save the lectures about being too influenced.

267
00:12:48,797 --> 00:12:49,337
You're wrong.

268
00:12:49,337 --> 00:12:56,617
Lately, I feel like I understand you, but I still think it's enormously dangerous here.

269
00:12:57,417 --> 00:13:00,657
The common sense of this world doesn't completely mesh with our understanding.

270
00:13:01,117 --> 00:13:02,317
It's not how we were created.

271
00:13:02,677 --> 00:13:03,577
Never forget that.

272
00:13:03,957 --> 00:13:06,757
Isn't it our differences that make living here so fun?

273
00:13:06,757 --> 00:13:09,137
I found you!

274
00:13:13,417 --> 00:13:16,697
Oh, you thought you were going to get away with that stunt, didn't you?

275
00:13:17,157 --> 00:13:20,577
You seem like you could hold your own, but maybe not while he's here.

276
00:13:21,137 --> 00:13:22,597
The strongest local delinquent.

277
00:13:22,757 --> 00:13:24,557
They call him the Dragon of Destruction.

278
00:13:25,097 --> 00:13:26,337
A woman, huh?

279
00:13:26,757 --> 00:13:30,497
I always say if you can put up a fight, it doesn't matter what your gender is.

280
00:13:30,497 --> 00:13:34,677
But if you can't fight, then I suggest you hurry up and apologize for wasting my time.

281
00:13:34,957 --> 00:13:36,457
Do you still think you can fight me?

282
00:13:36,877 --> 00:13:39,437
I hope you're not expecting any mercy!

283
00:13:40,517 --> 00:13:47,917
There are way too many of them.

284
00:13:48,137 --> 00:13:50,837
I guess I'll wear the dirty clothes Ms. Kobayashi gave me.

285
00:13:55,337 --> 00:13:58,317
If you don't understand by now, then you never will!

286
00:13:58,317 --> 00:14:01,597
You will never oppose me again!

287
00:14:05,657 --> 00:14:07,957
Will you shut up?

288
00:14:21,177 --> 00:14:21,777
Hmm?

289
00:14:23,037 --> 00:14:26,037
Good afternoon, Toru. You look lovely, Ms. Toru.

290
00:14:26,477 --> 00:14:26,957
Okay.

291
00:14:26,957 --> 00:14:29,197
You sure are popular today. What's up?

292
00:14:35,377 --> 00:14:38,097
Hey, Ryu, it's pretty late. Let's get out of here.

293
00:14:38,477 --> 00:14:40,717
You expect me to take being defeated lying down?

294
00:14:40,937 --> 00:14:43,157
I'll build my strength till I can get my revenge!

295
00:14:43,657 --> 00:14:44,597
Sounds good!

296
00:14:44,857 --> 00:14:46,237
There's a bear!

297
00:14:49,617 --> 00:14:52,197
Perfect! Now you'll see how strong I've become!

298
00:14:52,197 --> 00:15:11,657
I want to go to an amusement park!

299
00:15:11,657 --> 00:15:18,697
I've never understood those places where people pay to stand in line all day just to make themselves throw up.

300
00:15:19,697 --> 00:15:22,137
Have you not been to an amusement park, Ms. Kobayashi?

301
00:15:22,137 --> 00:15:27,357
If that's the case, then I don't mind going with Kana and we can tell you all about it.

302
00:15:27,697 --> 00:15:31,577
Suddenly a dragon's going to mentor me on the way this world works? Yeah, no.

303
00:15:31,997 --> 00:15:35,657
I'll take you just this once, but only because I know so much about them.

304
00:15:35,817 --> 00:15:37,337
And you're wanting to learn!

305
00:15:38,137 --> 00:15:40,017
Can Psycho Replace come with us, too?

306
00:15:40,017 --> 00:15:40,577
Why not?

307
00:15:43,057 --> 00:15:44,137
Well, we're here.

308
00:15:44,637 --> 00:15:45,897
What is this place?

309
00:15:46,257 --> 00:15:48,297
It's hard to believe we're in the same country.

310
00:15:48,417 --> 00:15:50,497
Right? So this is the kind of place it is.

311
00:15:50,497 --> 00:15:50,637
Huh?

312
00:15:51,197 --> 00:15:52,497
Every time I come here!

313
00:15:53,157 --> 00:15:57,857
And therefore, when you encounter the unusual, you create fond memories for life.

314
00:15:58,117 --> 00:16:00,457
Just allow yourself to let go and forget your daily routines.

315
00:16:00,457 --> 00:16:01,717
I recognize that voice!

316
00:16:02,057 --> 00:16:02,577
Me too.

317
00:16:02,577 --> 00:16:07,477
Hello! I am your guide to this wacky world of dreams.

318
00:16:07,737 --> 00:16:10,777
In a way, this job could be considered a type of parlor maid.

319
00:16:10,977 --> 00:16:12,617
You don't think that's stretching it just a bit?

320
00:16:13,377 --> 00:16:13,817
Working?

321
00:16:14,337 --> 00:16:17,637
My father's friend runs this park and said they were kind of short-staffed.

322
00:16:17,697 --> 00:16:18,997
So I'm helping him out.

323
00:16:19,477 --> 00:16:20,077
Look at this.

324
00:16:20,337 --> 00:16:24,157
If you're hungry, there's a cafe in this area here that I think you'd really enjoy.

325
00:16:24,437 --> 00:16:25,837
Yeah? Thanks. We'll try it.

326
00:16:26,357 --> 00:16:29,217
Hello! I am Parkourland's Akro!

327
00:16:29,837 --> 00:16:31,577
Such a passionate employee.

328
00:16:32,577 --> 00:16:36,357
Kobayashi, I'm gonna go play with Saikawai and Ilulu.

329
00:16:36,677 --> 00:16:39,457
Okay. Meet back up at the Ferris wheel at four o'clock.

330
00:16:42,497 --> 00:16:44,117
All right. What do you want to do?

331
00:16:44,337 --> 00:16:47,337
I mean, just as adults all alone.

332
00:16:47,717 --> 00:16:50,317
Can't imagine what you'd want to do with that, but I'm intrigued.

333
00:16:51,837 --> 00:16:54,557
Huh. It's an entire room made out of mirrors.

334
00:16:54,997 --> 00:16:56,877
Weird. There are way too many means.

335
00:16:57,597 --> 00:17:00,897
What is the purpose of having mirrors covering every inch of the walls?

336
00:17:00,897 --> 00:17:04,617
The better to re-examine and re-evaluate your truest self, my dear.

337
00:17:05,077 --> 00:17:05,697
I see.

338
00:17:06,337 --> 00:17:10,557
I wonder if it's telling me that I'm supposed to accept my human form as my truest self.

339
00:17:11,417 --> 00:17:13,957
I have to say, you're conquering the maze pretty quickly.

340
00:17:14,237 --> 00:17:17,017
I can usually tell the way from the echoes of sound.

341
00:17:17,017 --> 00:17:18,497
You're kind of like a bat.

342
00:17:19,357 --> 00:17:21,557
I've come to curse you!

343
00:17:23,097 --> 00:17:25,257
I'm scared of costumes and props!

344
00:17:25,437 --> 00:17:28,057
Calm down, Saikawa. I'll protect you.

345
00:17:32,057 --> 00:17:37,597
I know this one. You spin the table.

346
00:17:38,077 --> 00:17:38,317
Huh?

347
00:17:38,317 --> 00:17:43,277
I'm trying to figure out why this is fun.

348
00:17:43,397 --> 00:17:45,577
It's called centrifugal force?

349
00:17:45,777 --> 00:17:50,437
Are you saying that humans enjoy physically experiencing a stronger rotational force

350
00:17:50,437 --> 00:17:53,917
in order to become more aware of the planet's natural rotation?

351
00:17:54,457 --> 00:17:57,097
Centrifugal force and rotational force aren't...

352
00:17:57,097 --> 00:17:58,417
You know what? Let's go with that.

353
00:17:58,617 --> 00:17:58,917
Yes.

354
00:17:59,277 --> 00:18:00,097
Let's go with what?

355
00:18:01,137 --> 00:18:02,897
Can I try spinning us around now?

356
00:18:03,157 --> 00:18:03,677
Yeah, sure.

357
00:18:03,677 --> 00:18:04,937
Here we go!

358
00:18:07,677 --> 00:18:09,657
What is this?

359
00:18:09,737 --> 00:18:10,757
How do we play with it?

360
00:18:15,157 --> 00:18:16,757
Yarn, this is so fun!

361
00:18:17,397 --> 00:18:19,117
The rock is spinning!

362
00:18:23,717 --> 00:18:26,237
Sorry. I didn't mean to do it again.

363
00:18:26,817 --> 00:18:28,637
Man, Psycho, you're pretty funny.

364
00:18:31,757 --> 00:18:33,437
This, too, is a maid's duty.

365
00:18:34,217 --> 00:18:35,557
A unicorn, huh?

366
00:18:36,297 --> 00:18:38,977
They're notorious for falling in love with virgins.

367
00:18:39,357 --> 00:18:40,997
Wow, are you saying this could be my moment?

368
00:18:41,637 --> 00:18:44,477
Don't joke about that. Your virginity belongs to me.

369
00:18:44,877 --> 00:18:45,317
Creepy.

370
00:18:46,197 --> 00:18:47,337
Would you like a snack?

371
00:18:48,397 --> 00:18:48,877
Lucky!

372
00:18:48,877 --> 00:18:50,577
Yes, thank you very much!

373
00:18:53,477 --> 00:18:55,297
Taco, is yours yummy, too?

374
00:18:55,517 --> 00:18:57,517
Oh, but I forgot to save you some.

375
00:18:57,657 --> 00:18:59,077
Sorry, Khan, I ate it all.

376
00:19:00,617 --> 00:19:02,377
You're right, that one's yummy, too.

377
00:19:02,377 --> 00:19:05,837
Wow, she held it back.

378
00:19:05,857 --> 00:19:08,037
I can show self-control when it really counts.

379
00:19:08,117 --> 00:19:09,677
Well, in that case, take this.

380
00:19:09,797 --> 00:19:10,877
One more, please.

381
00:19:14,677 --> 00:19:18,937
I had so much fun, Miss Kobayashi!

382
00:19:19,137 --> 00:19:20,777
I couldn't tell through all your complaining.

383
00:19:20,777 --> 00:19:25,897
As long as I'm with you, I'd have fun even in the depths of the darkest abyss where light can't reach!

384
00:19:26,117 --> 00:19:28,037
That doesn't sound like fun to me, Toru.

385
00:19:29,237 --> 00:19:33,337
But I guess I agree that fun is more about who you're with than where you are.

386
00:19:33,557 --> 00:19:36,717
And you had fun with me, didn't you, Miss Kobayashi? Admit it!

387
00:19:36,717 --> 00:19:40,177
I think the cafe Georgie mentioned should be around here somewhere.

388
00:19:43,457 --> 00:19:44,657
I know that outfit!

389
00:19:44,937 --> 00:19:48,337
That's the Victorian main style you told me you always admired since you were little!

390
00:19:49,297 --> 00:19:52,377
That's the best smile I've seen on her at any place we went today!

391
00:19:52,537 --> 00:19:53,037
Thank you.

392
00:19:53,417 --> 00:19:54,937
Thank you so much, Georgie.

393
00:19:55,197 --> 00:19:56,537
I mean, it tastes average.

394
00:19:56,957 --> 00:19:58,897
Not like I have anyone to drink it with, you know?

395
00:19:59,017 --> 00:20:00,937
I would think you'd drink it with me, wouldn't you?

396
00:20:00,937 --> 00:20:04,517
They're here somewhere.

397
00:20:05,077 --> 00:20:05,457
Hey.

398
00:20:06,017 --> 00:20:06,877
Are you okay?

399
00:20:07,317 --> 00:20:08,597
Yeah, I'm good.

400
00:20:09,137 --> 00:20:10,997
Choking up my own happiness, I guess.

401
00:20:12,797 --> 00:20:13,357
Georgie!

402
00:20:14,637 --> 00:20:16,977
You young ladies look like you're having fun.

403
00:20:17,597 --> 00:20:20,497
I can send you copies of the sweet photos I just took of you.

404
00:20:20,997 --> 00:20:23,117
I want to see now.

405
00:20:23,917 --> 00:20:25,217
Kobayashi, you're late!

406
00:20:25,577 --> 00:20:26,477
I'm so sorry.

407
00:20:27,057 --> 00:20:28,277
We lost track of time.

408
00:20:28,277 --> 00:20:31,297
So, shall we ride the Ferris wheel together?

409
00:20:35,497 --> 00:20:37,197
Did Georgie take all these photos?

410
00:20:37,877 --> 00:20:40,497
We were screaming because we were having a good time.

411
00:20:40,577 --> 00:20:43,197
I would love to live in a place that was always so much fun!

412
00:20:43,517 --> 00:20:45,997
Yeah, sorry my place is so ordinary and boring.

413
00:20:46,937 --> 00:20:48,097
What's the matter, Toru?

414
00:20:48,617 --> 00:20:50,737
I was just thinking about the rides.

415
00:20:51,277 --> 00:20:54,477
Ones that make sharp turns and rock back and forth make me nervous.

416
00:20:54,477 --> 00:20:59,977
Then there are the buildings with detailed designs and mascots modeled after fantastical beasts.

417
00:21:00,137 --> 00:21:01,397
She's feeling nostalgic?

418
00:21:01,777 --> 00:21:02,657
Wait a sec.

419
00:21:03,117 --> 00:21:04,177
We're in a simulator!

420
00:21:04,817 --> 00:21:06,297
Does it feel like riding a dragon?

421
00:21:06,457 --> 00:21:06,897
Ugh.

422
00:21:07,317 --> 00:21:10,497
Are they making these things to avoid riding dragons in real life?

423
00:21:10,777 --> 00:21:12,357
You and their disgusting monsters!

424
00:21:12,557 --> 00:21:14,517
How did you even jump to that interpretation?

425
00:21:14,517 --> 00:21:19,497
If you'd love me to take you everywhere, it'd be like going to your personal amusement park every day!

426
00:21:19,737 --> 00:21:21,297
That only has roller coasters!

427
00:21:22,557 --> 00:21:24,657
Although, maybe...

428
00:21:24,657 --> 00:21:27,197
Maybe I could do something like this every now and then.

429
00:21:27,857 --> 00:21:29,077
Nah, it's not good for the hips.

430
00:21:36,217 --> 00:21:36,697
Nye!

431
00:21:38,237 --> 00:21:38,677
Nye?

432
00:21:41,177 --> 00:21:41,617
Georgie!

433
00:21:41,617 --> 00:21:43,197
Oh, hi!

434
00:21:43,437 --> 00:21:44,557
Good morning to you ladies!

435
00:21:45,157 --> 00:21:46,157
What the...

436
00:21:46,157 --> 00:21:47,837
Did you forget your own name just now?

437
00:21:48,737 --> 00:21:49,097
Hm?

438
00:23:20,007 --> 00:23:22,007
Hi, Kanda's mom!

439
00:23:22,007 --> 00:23:24,007
I brought you the photos from the amusement park.

440
00:23:24,007 --> 00:23:26,007
There are thousands!

441
00:23:26,007 --> 00:23:27,007
Wow, that's a lot.

442
00:23:27,007 --> 00:23:29,007
It is? Then I'll go through all of them

443
00:23:29,007 --> 00:23:31,007
and only show you the best ones.

444
00:23:31,007 --> 00:23:33,007
Still a lot. Don't worry about it.

445
00:23:33,007 --> 00:23:35,007
I'm sure they're all amazing.

446
00:23:35,007 --> 00:23:38,007
This week on Who's Run?

447
00:23:38,007 --> 00:23:40,007
Pisces!

